{"lines": ["In January 1921, a five-masted schooner, the Carroll A. Deering, was bound for Norfolk, Virginia.", "At Barbados, her drunk first mate had said, \"I'll get the captain before we get to Norfolk, I will.\"", "He was arrested, but the captain forgave him and bailed him out.", "Weeks later, a lightship keeper off North Carolina saw the Deering pass.", "A red-haired man with a foreign accent shouted through a megaphone that they'd lost their anchors.", "He was not the captain, and the crew were milling about where they weren't allowed.", "The next afternoon, she was seen heading straight for Diamond Shoals with nobody on deck.", "She was found stuck fast on the shoals, with all sails set.", "Both lifeboats were gone, and the steering gear was smashed.", "In the galley, pots were still on the stove, from a meal of soup, spareribs and coffee.", "The only living things aboard were three half-starved cats.", "And the logbook, the ship's papers, and the navigation instruments were all gone.", "Five government departments investigated, and reached no official answer.", "And the last ship didn't just lose its crew, it couldn't even sink."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.12], ["January", 0.12, 0.32], ["1921,", 0.32, 1.68], ["a", 2.5, 2.7], ["five-masted", 2.7, 3.42], ["schooner,", 3.42, 4.04], ["the", 4.32, 4.38], ["Carroll", 4.38, 4.66], ["A.", 4.66, 4.98], ["Deering,", 5.28, 5.54], ["was", 5.94, 6.12], ["bound", 6.12, 6.42], ["for", 6.42, 6.76], ["Norfolk,", 6.76, 7.04], ["Virginia.", 7.44, 7.76], ["At", 8.38, 8.46], ["Barbados,", 8.46, 8.96], ["her", 9.42, 9.5], ["drunk", 9.5, 9.76], ["first", 9.76, 10.1], ["mate", 10.1, 10.4], ["had", 10.4, 10.58], ["said,", 10.58, 10.82], ["\"I'll", 11.28, 11.62], ["get", 11.62, 11.76], ["the", 11.76, 11.88], ["captain", 11.88, 12.2], ["before", 12.2, 12.52], ["we", 12.52, 12.76], ["get", 12.76, 12.9], ["to", 12.9, 13.06], ["Norfolk,", 13.06, 13.26], ["I", 13.78, 13.92], ["will.\"", 13.92, 14.62], ["He", 14.62, 14.84], ["was", 14.84, 